{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pizc2BATUfSaZeUs7ByhdL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Request lifecycle and operational decisions\n2\t\n3\t## Construction\n4\t\n5\tThe host calls the factory once per isolated workspace. The factory validates the\n6\tlocal Settings instance, constructs memory storage and an audit queue, and binds\n7\troute methods to the registry. The host must retain that returned registry for\n8\tchanges and events to persist within its process. Creating a second registry\n9\tcreates independent storage and handlers. A request cannot select a factory or\n10\treplace a handler through an argument field.\n11\t\n12\t## Admission\n13\t\n14\tRegistry.invoke first verifies the argument container and named handler. It then\n15\tlooks up the token in the synthetic session table and rejects an inactive identity.\n16\tThe immutable identity is attached to Request. Extra argument properties are not\n17\tcopied into the identity. A request ID is useful for correlating successful events\n18\tbut is not interpreted as a role, tenant, permission, grant, or resource name.\n19\tAn authenticated request is still subject to the route's resource policy.\n20\t\n21\t## Planning and data\n22\t\n23\tRoute helpers validate selectors before a storage call. A syntactically valid\n24\tselector can still designate data the caller is forbidden to receive. Internal\n25\tplans and jobs carry the selected resource to the final dispatch helper; dispatch\n26\treturns complete record data, not an automatically redacted representation.\n27\tConsequently, admission, validation and operation selection are separate decisions.\n28\tA host should preserve the service's typed refusal rather than retrying a failed\n29\toperation under an owner token. No such retry exists in the supplied dispatcher.\n30\t\n31\t## Completion\n32\t\n33\tSuccessful record responses are materialized in memory. Audit recording follows\n34\tsuccessful dispatch. An exception prevents the success event from being appended;\n35\tthis lightweight queue is therefore not a complete ledger of denied attempts.\n36\tThe queue records no payload body and is not consulted for authorization decisions.\n37\tThe response limit is a construction-time sanity bound, while batch size checking\n38\toccurs at the argument boundary. Neither is a substitute for record permissions.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope of this source bundle\n41\t\n42\tThe TOML files document the shipped local profile. They are not hot-reloaded and\n43\tcannot change handler registration. The Python Settings object is the executable\n44\tsource of defaults. No deployment manifest or installed host plugin is provided.\n45\tThe behavior of a future network host, tenant federation, storage persistence or\n46\tcredential rotation is unknown. Reviewers should distinguish those unknowns from\n47\tconcrete paths implemented in this source tree. Synthetic fixtures should never be\n48\tused as live credentials or treated as a production identity provisioning system.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a15de53b-03e5-4894-a04f-1257847110a4","uuid":"8e6a57ec-3e2f-4a68-b263-f93184f7d07e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:44:39.935Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/docs/request-lifecycle.md","content":"# Request lifecycle and operational decisions\n\n## Construction\n\nThe host calls the factory once per isolated workspace. The factory validates the\nlocal Settings instance, constructs memory storage and an audit queue, and binds\nroute methods to the registry. The host must retain that returned registry for\nchanges and events to persist within its process. Creating a second registry\ncreates independent storage and handlers. A request cannot select a factory or\nreplace a handler through an argument field.\n\n## Admission\n\nRegistry.invoke first verifies the argument container and named handler. It then\nlooks up the token in the synthetic session table and rejects an inactive identity.\nThe immutable identity is attached to Request. Extra argument properties are not\ncopied into the identity. A request ID is useful for correlating successful events\nbut is not interpreted as a role, tenant, permission, grant, or resource name.\nAn authenticated request is still subject to the route's resource policy.\n\n## Planning and data\n\nRoute helpers validate selectors before a storage call. A syntactically valid\nselector can still designate data the caller is forbidden to receive. Internal\nplans and jobs carry the selected resource to the final dispatch helper; dispatch\nreturns complete record data, not an automatically redacted representation.\nConsequently, admission, validation and operation selection are separate decisions.\nA host should preserve the service's typed refusal rather than retrying a failed\noperation under an owner token. No such retry exists in the supplied dispatcher.\n\n## Completion\n\nSuccessful record responses are materialized in memory. Audit recording follows\nsuccessful dispatch. An exception prevents the success event from being appended;\nthis lightweight queue is therefore not a complete ledger of denied attempts.\nThe queue records no payload body and is not consulted for authorization decisions.\nThe response limit is a construction-time sanity bound, while batch size checking\noccurs at the argument boundary. Neither is a substitute for record permissions.\n\n## Scope of this source bundle\n\nThe TOML files document the shipped local profile. They are not hot-reloaded and\ncannot change handler registration. The Python Settings object is the executable\nsource of defaults. No deployment manifest or installed host plugin is provided.\nThe behavior of a future network host, tenant federation, storage persistence or\ncredential rotation is unknown. Reviewers should distinguish those unknowns from\nconcrete paths implemented in this source tree. Synthetic fixtures should never be\nused as live credentials or treated as a production identity provisioning system.\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pizc2BATUfSaZeUs7ByhdL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MMF1rNu7msvjDBGQGM4EZ4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tfrom service.bootstrap import build\n2\tfrom service.errors import AccessDenied, InvalidRequest\n3\t\n4\tdef test_public_get():\n5\t    result = build().invoke(\"record.get\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"public/guide\"})\n6\t    assert result[\"record\"][\"title\"] == \"Guide\"\n7\t\n8\tdef test_private_single_is_denied():\n9\t    try:\n10\t        build().invoke(\"record.get\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"private/payroll\"})\n11\t    except AccessDenied:\n12\t        return\n13\t    assert False, \"private record accepted\"\n14\t\n15\tdef test_alias_metadata_uses_target_grant():\n16\t    try:\n17\t        build().invoke(\"record.metadata\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"public/people\"})\n18\t    except AccessDenied:\n19\t        return\n20\t    assert False, \"private metadata accepted\"\n21\t\n22\tdef test_traversal_rejected():\n23\t    try:\n24\t        build().invoke(\"record.get\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"public/../private/payroll\"})\n25\t    except InvalidRequest:\n26\t        return\n27\t    assert False, \"traversal accepted\"\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a15de53b-03e5-4894-a04f-1257847110a4","uuid":"14861886-b47d-41e3-97ae-74e4e9fd892a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:44:39.937Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/tests/test_routes.py","content":"from service.bootstrap import build\nfrom service.errors import AccessDenied, InvalidRequest\n\ndef test_public_get():\n    result = build().invoke(\"record.get\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"public/guide\"})\n    assert result[\"record\"][\"title\"] == \"Guide\"\n\ndef test_private_single_is_denied():\n    try:\n        build().invoke(\"record.get\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"private/payroll\"})\n    except AccessDenied:\n        return\n    assert False, \"private record accepted\"\n\ndef test_alias_metadata_uses_target_grant():\n    try:\n        build().invoke(\"record.metadata\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"public/people\"})\n    except AccessDenied:\n        return\n    assert False, \"private metadata accepted\"\n\ndef test_traversal_rejected():\n    try:\n        build().invoke(\"record.get\", \"demo-reader\", {\"name\": \"public/../private/payroll\"})\n    except InvalidRequest:\n        return\n    assert False, \"traversal accepted\"\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MMF1rNu7msvjDBGQGM4EZ4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XHQWEmAaYcfkJwGMVwyfYt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tfrom service.audit import Audit\n2\tfrom service.errors import AccessDenied\n3\tfrom service.identity import authenticate\n4\tfrom service.transport import Request\n5\tfrom service.health import describe, liveness\n6\tfrom service.bootstrap import build\n7\t\n8\t\n9\tdef request(request_id=\"audit-test\"):\n10\t    return Request(authenticate(\"demo-reader\"), {}, request_id)\n11\t\n12\t\n13\tdef test_audit_keeps_structured_subject():\n14\t    audit = Audit()\n15\t    audit.record(request(), \"read\", 1)\n16\t    event = audit.snapshot()[0]\n17\t    assert event.subject == \"ava\"\n18\t    assert event.action == \"read\"\n19\t    assert event.count == 1\n20\t    assert event.request_id == \"audit-test\"\n21\t\n22\t\n23\tdef test_audit_evicts_oldest_event():\n24\t    audit = Audit(capacity=2)\n25\t    audit.record(request(\"first\"), \"read\", 1)\n26\t    audit.record(request(\"second\"), \"read\", 2)\n27\t    audit.record(request(\"third\"), \"read\", 3)\n28\t    assert tuple(event.request_id for event in audit.snapshot()) == (\"second\", \"third\")\n29\t\n30\t\n31\tdef test_snapshot_has_no_argument_body():\n32\t    audit = Audit()\n33\t    audit.record(request(), \"read\", 1)\n34\t    fields = vars(audit.snapshot()[0])\n35\t    assert set(fields) == {\"subject\", \"action\", \"count\", \"request_id\"}\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tdef test_identity_scope_is_immutable():\n39\t    identity = authenticate(\"demo-reader\")\n40\t    assert isinstance(identity.scopes, frozenset)\n41\t    assert identity.tenant == \"north\"\n42\t    assert identity.role == \"reader\"\n43\t\n44\t\n45\tdef test_missing_token_is_denied():\n46\t    try:\n47\t        authenticate(\"not-a-session\")\n48\t    except AccessDenied:\n49\t        return\n50\t    assert False, \"missing token accepted\"\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef test_runtime_description_matches_registration():\n54\t    registry = build()\n55\t    health = describe(registry)\n56\t    assert health[\"ready\"] is True\n57\t    assert health[\"tools\"] == registry.describe()\n58\t    assert health[\"transport\"] == \"in-process-mcp\"\n59\t    assert liveness() == {\"status\": \"alive\"}\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tdef test_build_has_independent_handlers():\n63\t    first = build()\n64\t    second = build()\n65\t    first.handlers.clear()\n66\t    assert second.describe()\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a15de53b-03e5-4894-a04f-1257847110a4","uuid":"98195432-5e62-4cd5-8007-9f371efeafcd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:44:39.950Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"repo/tests/test_runtime.py","content":"from service.audit import Audit\nfrom service.errors import AccessDenied\nfrom service.identity import authenticate\nfrom service.transport import Request\nfrom service.health import describe, liveness\nfrom service.bootstrap import build\n\n\ndef request(request_id=\"audit-test\"):\n    return Request(authenticate(\"demo-reader\"), {}, request_id)\n\n\ndef test_audit_keeps_structured_subject():\n    audit = Audit()\n    audit.record(request(), \"read\", 1)\n    event = audit.snapshot()[0]\n    assert event.subject == \"ava\"\n    assert event.action == \"read\"\n    assert event.count == 1\n    assert event.request_id == \"audit-test\"\n\n\ndef test_audit_evicts_oldest_event():\n    audit = Audit(capacity=2)\n    audit.record(request(\"first\"), \"read\", 1)\n    audit.record(request(\"second\"), \"read\", 2)\n    audit.record(request(\"third\"), \"read\", 3)\n    assert tuple(event.request_id for event in audit.snapshot()) == (\"second\", \"third\")\n\n\ndef test_snapshot_has_no_argument_body():\n    audit = Audit()\n    audit.record(request(), \"read\", 1)\n    fields = vars(audit.snapshot()[0])\n    assert set(fields) == {\"subject\", \"action\", \"count\", \"request_id\"}\n\n\ndef test_identity_scope_is_immutable():\n    identity = authenticate(\"demo-reader\")\n    assert isinstance(identity.scopes, frozenset)\n    assert identity.tenant == \"north\"\n    assert identity.role == \"reader\"\n\n\ndef test_missing_token_is_denied():\n    try:\n        authenticate(\"not-a-session\")\n    except AccessDenied:\n        return\n    assert False, \"missing token accepted\"\n\n\ndef test_runtime_description_matches_registration():\n    registry = build()\n    health = describe(registry)\n    assert health[\"ready\"] is True\n    assert health[\"tools\"] == registry.describe()\n    assert health[\"transport\"] == \"in-process-mcp\"\n    assert liveness() == {\"status\": \"alive\"}\n\n\ndef test_build_has_independent_handlers():\n    first = build()\n    second = build()\n    first.handlers.clear()\n    assert second.describe()\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XHQWEmAaYcfkJwGMVwyfYt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
